      "side": 1,
      "message": "Verified on lemonadep (op9 pro).\n\nDevice:\nLemonadep (op9 pro) with lineage-23.2 and MindTheGapps-16\n\nSteps:\n- Make changes to system/core/rootdir/etc/hosts and build the system image and update package. (Did it this way to make sure the changes aren\u0027t just due to overlayfs)\n- Trigger an OTA with push-update.sh.\n- Verify changes in /system/etc/hosts via ADB.\n- Undo changes in the source tree and rebuild.\n- Trigger another OTA.\n- Changes in /system/etc/hosts should still be present even though it was removed from the sources.\n\nThese steps ensure that 50-lineage.sh is backing up and restoring /system/etc/hosts correctly. GApps are also persisted across OTAs but that seems to be covered by 30-gapps.sh.\n\nNote- It\u0027s a little odd that 50-lineage.sh has mode 644 (Was the same before). 30-gapps.sh has executable permissions, so maybe this can be done for 50-lineage.sh too in a future commit.",
      "revId": "66fbae27f1ec37ea0eb08d1bcd980474bfc053cf",
      "serverId": "1ec6b3db-b2c1-4fa4-84a2-4c7efe89ba71"
    },
